> Module Student_loan_adjustment

# Student loan interest deduction (Schedule 1 line 21)

Direct File module `studentLoanAdjustment.xml`, with the modified AGI of
`taxCalculations.xml` `/magiForStudentLoanInterestDeduction`. Issue #24. Tests
are in `catala/tests/test_student_loan_adjustment.catala_en`; the oracle
comparison is `make difftest SCOPE=student_loan_adjustment`
(`difftest/mappings/student_loan_adjustment.mjs`).

> Using Types
> Using Params_2024 as P
> Using Rounding as R

## 26 U.S.C. § 221 Interest on education loans

### (a) Allowance of deduction

"In the case of an individual, there shall be allowed as a deduction for the
taxable year an amount equal to the interest paid by the taxpayer during the
taxable year on any qualified education loan." (`sources/statute/irc-221.html`)

### (b) Maximum deduction

"(1) In general. Except as provided in paragraph (2), the deduction allowed by
subsection (a) for the taxable year shall not exceed $2,500." This is
`P.student_loan_interest_cap`.

"(2)(A) In general. The amount which would (but for this paragraph) be
allowable as a deduction under this section shall be reduced (but not below
zero) by the amount determined under subparagraph (B). (B) Amount of
reduction. The amount determined under this subparagraph is the amount which
bears the same ratio to the amount which would be so taken into account as—
(i) the excess of— (I) the taxpayer's modified adjusted gross income for such
taxable year, over (II) $50,000 ($100,000 in the case of a joint return),
bears to (ii) $15,000 ($30,000 in the case of a joint return)."

The $50,000 and $100,000 are indexed by § 221(f). For TY2024 "the $2,500
maximum deduction for interest paid on qualified education loans under § 221
begins to phase out under § 221(b)(2)(B), as adjusted for inflation, for
taxpayers with modified adjusted gross income in excess of $80,000 ($165,000
for joint returns), and is completely phased out for taxpayers with modified
adjusted gross income of $95,000 or more ($195,000 or more for joint returns)"
(Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.30, `sources/revproc/rp-23-34.pdf` p 16). The four
figures are `P.student_loan_phaseout_*`; the ranges $15,000 and $30,000 are the
differences end minus start.

### (c) Dependents not eligible for deduction

"No deduction shall be allowed by this section to an individual for the taxable
year if a deduction under section 151 with respect to such individual is
allowed to another taxpayer".

### (e)(2) Married couples must file joint return

"If the taxpayer is married at the close of the taxable year, the deduction
shall be allowed under subsection (a) only if the taxpayer and the taxpayer's
spouse file a joint return for the taxable year." Married filing separately is
therefore disallowed.

## Student Loan Interest Deduction Worksheet, Schedule 1 line 21

(`sources/forms-instructions/i1040gi--2024.pdf` p 94; the filing-status rules
are on the preceding page.) Lines of the worksheet and the facts that compute
them:

1. "Enter the total interest you paid in 2024 on qualified student loans ...
   Don't enter more than $2,500": `LesserOf(interest, 2500)`.
2. "Enter the amount from Form 1040 or 1040-SR, line 9": `/totalIncome`.
3. "Enter the total of the amounts from Schedule 1, lines 11 through 20, and 23
   and 25": `/adjustmentsToIncomeExcludingStudentLoanInterest`.
4. "Subtract line 3 from line 2": the modified AGI.
5. "$80,000 ... Married filing jointly $165,000."
6. "Is the amount on line 4 more than the amount on line 5? No. Skip lines 6 and
   7, enter -0- on line 8 ... Yes. Subtract line 5 from line 4."
7. "Divide line 6 by $15,000 ($30,000 if married filing jointly). Enter the
   result as a decimal (rounded to at least three places). If the result is
   1.000 or more, enter 1.000."
8. "Multiply line 1 by line 7."
9. "Student loan interest deduction. Subtract line 8 from line 1."

## Direct File's three-decimal ratio is not followed (DF-BUG(7), candidate)

IRC 221(b)(2)(B) reduces the deduction by "the amount which bears the same
ratio to the amount which would be so taken into account as" excess MAGI over
the range: the exact fraction. Worksheet line 7 asks for the ratio "rounded to
at least three places". Direct File stores every `Dollar` at two decimals, so
`/studentLoanAmountPhaseOutAmount` computes

    phase_out = ( ( (10 * excess) / range ) * capped_interest ) / 10

with three `HALF_EVEN` roundings to the cent (`types/Dollar.scala`): the ratio
is cut to exactly three decimals, then the product and the quotient are each
rounded again. Rounding the ratio to three decimals is allowed by the form
("at least three") but is not the statute's exact ratio, and it moves the
result by up to $2 (see the tests and the pull request). Under the project
policy (CONVENTIONS section 8: the statute wins, engine rounding artefacts are
computed exactly) this module computes the exact fraction and rounds once, at
line 21, to the whole dollar. At MAGI $87,500 single the ratio is exactly 1/2
and both readings agree on $1,250; at $85,000 single the statute gives
$2,500 - $833.33 = $1,666.67, i.e. $1,667, and Direct File $1,668.

`df_phase_out_amount` is Direct File's computation, kept only so the tests
can show the divergence; the scope does not use it. It uses
`round_half_even_cents`.

```catala-metadata
## `value` (in dollars, exact) rounded to the cent with `HALF_EVEN`: ties go to
## the even cent, like Java `RoundingMode.HALF_EVEN` in DF `Dollar.apply`.
## Used only by `df_phase_out_amount`.
declaration round_half_even_cents content money
  depends on value content decimal
  equals
    let cents equals value * 100.0 in
    let below equals Decimal.round_by_default of cents in
    let fraction equals cents - below in
    let even_cents equals
      if fraction < 0.5 then below
      else if fraction > 0.5 then below + 1.0
      else if (Decimal.truncate of (below / 2.0)) * 2.0 = below then below
      else below + 1.0
    in
    $0.01 * even_cents

## Direct File's `/studentLoanAmountPhaseOutAmount` for an excess over the
## phase-out start, the range and the capped interest. Reference for tests
## only; it is the DF-BUG(7) behaviour and is not what the scope computes.
declaration df_phase_out_amount content money
  depends on
    excess content money,
    range content money,
    capped_interest content money
  equals
    let ratio_times_ten equals
      round_half_even_cents of ((excess * 10.0) / range) in
    let product equals
      round_half_even_cents of ((ratio_times_ten / $1) * (capped_interest / $1)) in
    round_half_even_cents of ((product / $1) / 10.0)

## The statute's phase-out (IRC 221(b)(2)(B)): the capped interest times
## excess / range, to the cent (display value; line 21 rounds the exact value).
declaration exact_phase_out_amount content money
  depends on
    excess content money,
    range content money,
    capped_interest content money
  equals
    capped_interest * (excess / range)
```

## The scope

```catala-metadata
## Schedule 1 line 21. DF: studentLoanAdjustment.xml.
declaration scope StudentLoanAdjustment:
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /filingStatus (Writable)
  input filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  # DF: studentLoanAdjustment.xml /hadStudentLoanInterestPayments (Writable)
  input had_student_loan_interest_payments condition
  # DF: studentLoanAdjustment.xml /studentLoansQualify (Writable)
  input student_loans_qualify condition
  # DF: studentLoanAdjustment.xml /studentLoanInterestAmount (Writable)
  input student_loan_interest_amount content money
  # DF: filers.xml /isMFJDependent, from Filers.is_mfj_dependent
  input is_mfj_dependent condition
  # DF: filers.xml /eitherFilerIsClaimedAsDependent, from Filers
  input either_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent condition
  # DF: income.xml /totalIncome (Form 1040 line 9)
  input total_income content money
  # DF: taxCalculations.xml /adjustmentsToIncomeExcludingStudentLoanInterest
  # (Schedule 1 lines 11 to 20, 23 and 25: educator expenses plus HSA deduction)
  input adjustments_to_income_excluding_student_loan_interest content money

  # DF: filingStatus.xml /isFilingStatusMFJ
  internal is_filing_status_mfj condition
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /isFilingStatusMFS
  internal is_filing_status_mfs condition
  # Worksheet line 4. DF: taxCalculations.xml /magiForStudentLoanInterestDeduction
  output magi_for_student_loan_interest_deduction content money
  # DF: /incomeTooHighForStudentLoanInterestDeductionNotMFJ
  output income_too_high_not_mfj condition
  # DF: /incomeTooHighForStudentLoanInterestDeductionMFJ
  output income_too_high_mfj condition
  # DF: /cannotDeductStudentLoanInterestBecauseIncomeOrFilingStatus
  output cannot_deduct_because_income_or_filing_status condition
  # DF: /cannotDeductStudentLoanInterestBecauseDependents
  output cannot_deduct_because_dependents condition
  # DF: /cannotDeductStudentLoanInterestBecauseLoansDontQualify
  output cannot_deduct_because_loans_dont_qualify condition
  # DF: /cannotDeductStudentLoanInterest
  output cannot_deduct_student_loan_interest condition
  # Worksheet line 1. DF: LesserOf(/studentLoanInterestAmount, /maxStudentLoadDeduction)
  internal capped_interest content money
  # Worksheet line 5, and the denominator of line 7.
  # DF: /studentLoanPhaseOutStart(Mfj), /studentLoanPhaseOutRange(Mfj)
  internal phase_out_start content money
  internal phase_out_range content money
  # Worksheet line 6 (zero when line 4 is not above line 5)
  internal excess_over_phase_out_start content money
  # Worksheet line 7, exact: excess / range, at most 1 (decimal, not rounded)
  internal phase_out_ratio content decimal
  # Worksheet line 8, to the cent for display. DF: /studentLoanAmountPhaseOutAmount
  output student_loan_amount_phase_out_amount content money
  # Schedule 1 line 21. DF: /studentLoanInterestAdjustmentAmount
  output student_loan_interest_adjustment_amount content money
  # DF: /isReceivingStudentLoanInterestAdjustment
  output is_receiving_student_loan_interest_adjustment condition
```

## Modified AGI and the income limit

```catala
scope StudentLoanAdjustment:
  definition is_filing_status_mfj equals filing_status = MarriedFilingJointly
  definition is_filing_status_mfs equals filing_status = MarriedFilingSeparately

  # Worksheet lines 2 to 4, i1040gi--2024.pdf p 94.
  # DF: /magiForStudentLoanInterestDeduction
  definition magi_for_student_loan_interest_deduction equals
    total_income - adjustments_to_income_excluding_student_loan_interest

  # Rev. Proc. 2023-34 p 16: "$95,000 or more" is fully phased out. DF tests
  # `magi > 95,000` and lets the phase-out reach 100 percent at 95,000 itself.
  # DF: /incomeTooHighForStudentLoanInterestDeductionNotMFJ
  definition income_too_high_not_mfj equals
    (not is_filing_status_mfj)
    and magi_for_student_loan_interest_deduction
        > P.student_loan_phaseout_end_other

  # DF: /incomeTooHighForStudentLoanInterestDeductionMFJ
  definition income_too_high_mfj equals
    is_filing_status_mfj
    and magi_for_student_loan_interest_deduction
        > P.student_loan_phaseout_end_joint
```

## Who cannot take the deduction

IRC 221(e)(2): married filing separately is out. IRC 221(c) and the worksheet
text: a filer (or spouse) claimed as a dependent is out. The loans must
qualify (§ 221(d)(1)).

```catala
scope StudentLoanAdjustment:
  # IRC 221(e)(2), 221(b)(2).
  # DF: /cannotDeductStudentLoanInterestBecauseIncomeOrFilingStatus
  definition cannot_deduct_because_income_or_filing_status equals
    is_filing_status_mfs or income_too_high_not_mfj or income_too_high_mfj

  # IRC 221(c). DF: /cannotDeductStudentLoanInterestBecauseDependents
  definition cannot_deduct_because_dependents equals
    (not cannot_deduct_because_income_or_filing_status)
    and either_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent

  # IRC 221(d)(1). DF: /cannotDeductStudentLoanInterestBecauseLoansDontQualify
  definition cannot_deduct_because_loans_dont_qualify equals
    (not cannot_deduct_because_income_or_filing_status)
    and had_student_loan_interest_payments
    and (not either_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent)
    and (not student_loans_qualify)

  # DF: /cannotDeductStudentLoanInterest
  definition cannot_deduct_student_loan_interest equals
    cannot_deduct_because_dependents
    or cannot_deduct_because_loans_dont_qualify
    or cannot_deduct_because_income_or_filing_status
    or is_mfj_dependent
```

## Worksheet lines 1 to 9

```catala
scope StudentLoanAdjustment:
  # Worksheet line 1, IRC 221(b)(1)
  definition capped_interest equals
    Money.min of student_loan_interest_amount, P.student_loan_interest_cap

  # Worksheet line 5
  definition phase_out_start equals
    if is_filing_status_mfj then P.student_loan_phaseout_start_joint
    else P.student_loan_phaseout_start_other

  # IRC 221(b)(2)(B)(ii): $15,000 ($30,000 joint).
  # DF: /studentLoanPhaseOutRange(Mfj)
  definition phase_out_range equals
    if is_filing_status_mfj
    then P.student_loan_phaseout_end_joint - P.student_loan_phaseout_start_joint
    else P.student_loan_phaseout_end_other - P.student_loan_phaseout_start_other

  # Worksheet line 6: "No. Skip ... enter -0-" when line 4 is not above line 5
  definition excess_over_phase_out_start equals
    Money.max of $0,
      (magi_for_student_loan_interest_deduction - phase_out_start)

  # Worksheet line 7. IRC 221(b)(2)(B): the exact ratio, capped at 1.
  # DF-BUG(7): DF rounds this ratio to three decimals through a x10 trick with
  # HALF_EVEN cent roundings (`df_phase_out_amount`); not reproduced.
  definition phase_out_ratio equals
    Decimal.min of 1.0, (excess_over_phase_out_start / phase_out_range)

  # Worksheet line 8, display value. DF: /studentLoanAmountPhaseOutAmount
  definition student_loan_amount_phase_out_amount equals
    capped_interest * phase_out_ratio

  # Worksheet line 9, Sch 1 line 21: one rounding to the whole dollar of the
  # exact value, as DF's final `Round` (CONVENTIONS: R.round_dollar_exact).
  # DF: /studentLoanInterestAdjustmentAmount
  definition student_loan_interest_adjustment_amount equals
    if cannot_deduct_student_loan_interest
       or (not had_student_loan_interest_payments)
    then $0
    else R.round_dollar_exact of capped_interest, (1.0 - phase_out_ratio)

  # DF: /isReceivingStudentLoanInterestAdjustment
  definition is_receiving_student_loan_interest_adjustment equals
    student_loan_interest_adjustment_amount > $0
```
